  "answer": "Based on the NAWE website, **Writing in Education Vol. 33 – \"Writing & Location\"** contains 10 articles with the following authors:\n\n**Main article authors:**\n1. **Bryan Podmore** — *A Risky Business This Writing?* (elicits responses from Susan Wicks, Michelene Wandor, Gillian Allnutt, and Graham Mort)\n2. **Sarah Wardle** — *Audere Est Facere* and *Reflections on Memory and Identity*\n3. **Martin Goodman** — *Location and Dislocation – a Writer's Use of Place*\n4. **Fred Sedgwick** — *Primary Children Writing in the Grip of Shakespeare*\n5. **Paul Munden** — *Text and Context*\n6. **Maggie Butt** — *The View from Here*\n7. **Keith Bennett** — *Welcome to Maribor*\n8. **Carl Tighe** — *Worlds in War: War in Words*\n\n**Respondents to Podmore's article** (also contributors):\n- Susan Wicks\n- Michelene Wandor\n- Gillian Allnutt\n- Graham Mort\n\nSo **12 named contributors** in total: 8 primary article authors plus 4 respondents.\n\n## Sources\n- https://www.nawe.co.uk/DB/wie-editions/editions/writing-and-location.html",
